Package: SparseMSE
Title: 'Multiple Systems Estimation for Sparse Capture Data'
Version: 2.0.2
Authors@R: c(
  person("Lax", "Chan", email = "laxchan77@gmail.com", role = c("aut")),
  person("Bernard W.", "Silverman", email = "bernard.silverman@stats.ox.ac.uk", role = c("aut","cre")),
  person("Kyle", "Vincent", email = "kyle.shane.vincent@gmail.com", role= c("aut")))
Description: Provides multiple systems estimation methods for sparse capture data,
    including cases with non-overlapping lists and boundary estimates. The package
    is deprecated and has been superseded by 'MultipleSystemsEstimation', which
    should be used for current development and support. The methods were developed
    and analysed by Chan, Silverman and Vincent (2019)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1902.05156>.
URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.05156
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown
Imports: lpSolve, Rcapture
NeedsCompilation: no
